{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/57341-spoofing-and-aether","id":57341,"title":"Spoofing and Aether","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-25T03:26:09-08:00","id":57341,"title":"Spoofing and Aether","content":"I'm not sure of the abrangence of Spoofing. Can spoofing work against passive senses? For instance, can I spoof another demon's aether sense? Or cryptid, for that matter? It's a mystic sense, so it should, by the description (bye, bye hounding cryptids). But if did, how would any demon ever find another, if they are not going demon shape?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T09:45:58-08:00","id":57477,"title":"","content":"Well, Aetheric Resonance is an activated power, since you actually need to consciously do it. And spend aether - not exactly a plentiful resource to begin with.<br /> <br /> Still, spoofing should work against it. Why? Demon is a game of spies and intrigue. If a spy doesn't want to be found, then he should not be found. <br /> <br /> That said, the actual write up of Spoof uses the word &quot;may.&quot; Meaning, spoofing is optional. So, a demon can choose not to be spoofing so that a fellow demon can meet up. Demons tend to also carry around gadgets and aetheric stock piles, which I'm fairly sure don't fall under Spoofing. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, how do demons meet up? Cross paths on the job investigating Infrastructure, perhaps. A communication network among rings isn't too uncommon. Run into each other in similar interest zones - two Tempters working the same high society circuit almost certainly will meet eventually, while two Saboteurs in the arms trade likely run into each other as well. Be present when an angel falls, and head to the 'crash' site. There's an embed that lets you listen in on the god machine and 'over hear' it, even when it sends angels after another demon. There's stigmatics, who seem to get visions that lead you to other demons. <br /> <br /> And that's just off the top my head. I'm sure there's others. And its very easy to do the friend-of-a-friend thing from there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T09:55:10-08:00","id":57483,"title":"","content":"By my reading, Spoofing doesn't work against Aetheric Resonance because they don't interact at all. All Aetheric Resonance does is register if anyone in the area is spending Essence or Aether or otherwise giving it off. If a demon stays in cover, acts normal and doesn't do anything, then they register as non-Aetheric, no issue. If they switch to demon form, use an Exploit, activate their own Aetheric Resonance, etc. then they're going to be giving that off, and Spoofing isn't going to matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":451,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","user":"Kirby Jerusalem","date":". 01-25-2014, 01:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T10:26:38-08:00","id":57503,"title":"","content":"Well, from what I've read, it seems that Aetheric Resonance detects sources of Aether; it doesn't have to be actively spent or used in some way. Aetheric Resonance, for instance, would detect an item being used as a stock pile.<br /> <br /> That said, Demons carry aether in them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T10:48:42-08:00","id":57515,"title":"","content":"Stockpiles still radiate a miniscule amount of Aether. Demons in cover do not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pg. 184</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being in a Twilight state does not protect an angel from aetheric resonance, but demons hidden by Cover and angels masked by Infrastructure are not immediately revealed. This defense lapses only briefly when they expend Aether or Essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T16:02:57-08:00","id":57713,"title":"","content":"Well, if spoofing as described works against any power that would reveal the Demon as a supernatural being. There's no provision for activated powers and so on. It also works on powers that would give away the Demon's nature by implication. So, as written, even if a Demon spends Aether, he would use spoof to conceal it (it's reflexive and doesn't need the user to be aware of any attempt to find the Demon for it to work). <br /> <br /> Perhaps it just didn't have to work so well, as it makes very hard to justify that a group of Demons would get out of cover to get together, otherwise. They seem too paranoid to go looking for other Demons, if they have no way of knowing if they are humans, demons or angels in disguise. Even knowing that other Demons are Demons, it's still almost too risky to blow your cover, anyway. What with all those turn coats and psychos! <br /> <br /> *Spoiler alert*<br /> <br /> Its just that in the adventure, the ghost character seems to know the BB demonic nature and the play's just by looking. It's somewhat jarring, given the rules as written. Why don't the GMC put ghosts in all their installations? It seems too easy! <br /> <br /> But if Demons can hide so damn well, it makes hard to get them to interact. I get that ther has to be a way of making conflict work. <br /> <br /> *End Spoiler*<br /> <br /> Perhaps patching the spoofing by saying that it just doesn't work against other Demons is a better solution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T16:22:07-08:00","id":57729,"title":"","content":"I think that if Spoofing protects you from Aetheric Resonance, that would have been noted in the Aetheric Resonance write-up.<br /> <br /> Cover already protects you against a Demon using Aetheric Resonance, unless you spend Aether. As this is already somewhat like Spoofing, I'd say also allowing a Demon to Spoof this ability seems somewhat redundant and gives the Demon too much protection.<br /> <br /> EDIT: In other words, I agree with Kirby. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":304,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","user":"Penta","date":". 01-25-2014, 07:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T16:26:36-08:00","id":57735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/57341-spoofing-and-aether?p=57713#post57713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They seem too paranoid to go looking for other Demons, if they have no way of knowing if they are humans, demons or angels in disguise.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what they're aiming for, by the way. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T05:41:09-08:00","id":58643,"title":"","content":"I don't think spoofing can protect against being detected by Aetheric Resonance because spoofing only protects against you being detected as a demon, and Aetheric Resonance does not detect you as a demon, it detects that something nonspecific in the area used Aether.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1105-hulsmanm","name":"hulsmanm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T10:32:40-08:00","id":58857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/57341-spoofing-and-aether?p=57483#post57483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By my reading, Spoofing doesn't work against Aetheric Resonance because they don't interact at all. All Aetheric Resonance does is register if anyone in the area is spending Essence or Aether or otherwise giving it off. If a demon stays in cover, acts normal and doesn't do anything, then they register as non-Aetheric, no issue. If they switch to demon form, use an Exploit, activate their own Aetheric Resonance, etc. then they're going to be giving that off, and Spoofing isn't going to matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, when you are using an exploit in cover, as written, spoofing would work, yes. You get to roll against any supernatural detection that would single you out as a supernatural creature.<br /> <br /> And that's the thing. Unless you are going out of cover, there's no other way of other demons to know you are one of theirs. It makes very hard to justify for agencies, or even goups of demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T10:55:19-08:00","id":58891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/57341-spoofing-and-aether?p=58857#post58857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's the thing. Unless you are going out of cover, there's no other way of other demons to know you are one of theirs. It makes very hard to justify for agencies, or even goups of demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no way of knowing that none of the people I go to work with are serial murderers. Should I starve to death or be arrested for vagrancy when my money runs out rather than take that risk?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T11:27:54-08:00","id":58931,"title":"","content":"Trust is always risky, but it's preferable to the alternatives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T11:30:19-08:00","id":58934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/57341-spoofing-and-aether?p=58931#post58931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trust is always risky, but it's preferable to the alternatives.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know until you're wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T12:05:31-08:00","id":58978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/57341-spoofing-and-aether?p=57735#post57735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is what they're aiming for, by the way.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems that the developers want to have a demon community, given the Agencies and demons groups. So, they can't be *completely* paranoid. The Seattle setting and adventure make that demons, at least, know who are the players. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no way of knowing that none of the people I go to work with are serial murderers. Should I starve to death or be arrested for vagrancy when my money runs out rather than take that risk?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are a wanted spy in enemy territory, yes, you will keep it to yourself. The only way to know if someone else is a spy too is breaking cover, and that's suicidal (every mistake is a compromise). Also, if there is a way to spoof effectively even exploits, how will you starve? <br /> <br /> \u200bBetter if demons can feel when other demons are using Aether, even if spoof, by the RAW, should block that. At least it's a vanishing chance of a demon knowing that there's someone like him. Even if he can't be sure of his allegiance, that's a start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T12:07:31-08:00","id":58980,"title":"","content":"You'd have to be phenomenally wrong in order to be completely in a corner, speaking in the general sense. Certainly, there are moments where you'd be pretty screwed but if you can squeeze out of it as PC's regularly do, the odds of having no one being on your side is slim.<br /> <br /> Contrast that with just never exercising trust, where even if you get out of a pickle, you're going to have to rely on a lot of luck to get someone with the right principles to help you out.<br /> <br /> Extending trust early beats earning trust when the shit has hit the fan, is what I'm saying. Just don't be a complete idiot about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T12:19:12-08:00","id":58992,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I can't find the quote but there's a Burn Notice soliloquy about how trusting no one gets you burnt out extremely fast, and that gets you killed.<br /> <br /> As to the inability to tell between human, demon and angel, I am not making up that it's a design goal. They wrote it in such a way to engender as many trust issues as they can, hence why Agencies are treated as extremely risky in the text. Outside of the most paranoid games the demons are still going to find people they can trust, but in general I feel the game works best when you treat rings like cells instead of parts of big hierarchies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":451,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","user":"Kirby Jerusalem","date":". 01-27-2014, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T16:19:01-08:00","id":59248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/57341-spoofing-and-aether?p=58980#post58980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'd have to be phenomenally wrong in order to be completely in a corner, speaking in the general sense. Certainly, there are moments where you'd be pretty screwed but if you can squeeze out of it as PC's regularly do, the odds of having no one being on your side is slim.<br /> <br /> Contrast that with just never exercising trust, where even if you get out of a pickle, you're going to have to rely on a lot of luck to get someone with the right principles to help you out.<br /> <br /> Extending trust early beats earning trust when the shit has hit the fan, is what I'm saying. Just don't be a complete idiot about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bBut extending trust to whom? The perfect liars that won't break cover because neither they nor you have any idea if are demons or angels, or mortals around? How do you approach that? See, for all you know, you are the only demon around, and the general aether in the region (if there is any aether on the region) is there because of essence use. This isn't like true spies in hostile territory, that at least have a homeland and an organization, and some starting ground. There's paranoia and there's complete, paranoia. <br /> <br /> You start completely alone, and have no common experience with anybody. And you are in hostile territory, with a force overwhelmingly more powerful just waiting for you to commit a mistake, any mistake. Unless there is a way to pierce this with some sort of assurance, I cannot see how a demon would start to break cover and see if he has just got lucky with this guy he's been talking to. And thus, no demonic society, it becomes a solo paranoia game. And that's not what the adventure, nor the setting, nor the Seattle setting, seem to sell. <br /> <br /> OTOH, I cannot see other supernaturals just breaking cover on sight automatically, as it's implied ghosts do (on the adventure). 'He's just like you are, says the ghost', no I don't think so!<br /> <br /> I am thinking about running the game, and I can see the potential for players turtling up completely. The way I see, it's better to take the vampire solution: a demon knows a demon when he sees one. All others can be spoofed. And that's it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T16:55:07-08:00","id":59277,"title":"","content":"Cool, hope that works for you. Personally, I'm going to keep the trust issues including the inability to tell each other apart, leave it up to the players to figure out how they know each other and why they'd work together (or at least associate) and tell the players OOC that they're going to have to be extra proactive because there isn't any Prince to appeal to, there isn't a list of rings in the area, and dealing with agencies can be risky. In other words, the players -are- the authority.<br /> <br /> There are potential allies out there to trust (or to manipulate), assets to cultivate and information to learn, but it's on the players to find all that. Demon society functionally doesn't really exist in most places, and it certainly doesn't owe you anything by dint of a shared rebellion against the God-Machine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T10:20:25-08:00","id":59932,"title":"","content":"There's paranoia, there's complete paranoia, and then there's &quot;Fuck this, this is stupid, let's take some shots&quot;<br /> <br /> Demons aren't blind, and they aren't stupid. They can apply their own habits to others and begin looking for incongruities. Demons and Angels can't always perfectly hide-if Demons could, compromise wouldn't be an issue, and if angels could, demons would really be fucked. So a demon is going to see something sooner and later, and they can act on it-follow them, find out information, and set something up.<br /> <br /> Every contact is a gamble, yes. You think you found a demon who could help, turns out it's a convincing angel, or a demon who'd have no problem screwing you over. But that's the nature of the game-you have to take some chances if you're gonna do anything but sit on your ass. And even if you do sit on your ass, Demonic nature demands inevitable changes in Cover. That might be covered by regular XP, but often times you'll need to make a pact, and that's a blip of standing the hell out, just enough for people to notice.<br /> <br /> Sooner or later, someone is going to see you, and regardless of them being friend or foe, the situation is in their hands. You might as well be proactive, take some chances, and try and make friends at gunpoint. That way, even if you did screw it up, you have more control over the scenario.<br /> <br /> Rebellion is a gamble. Someone who doesn't want to play the game should never have broken the rules in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T14:01:13-08:00","id":60112,"title":"","content":"It appears that there is some concern about how players get to know each other or how they can become engaged in a wider demon community (if one exists) <br /> <br /> There's a little section in the book which asks demons to consider who knows what about them at this time and it suggests that you leave yourself vulnerable, at least a tiny bit to help encourage RP. ...hrmm. Ah here it is. In the Cover section under Compromises you are directed to answer Five Questions about how your demon may have already been compromised. <br /> <br /> So the game takes it as a given that your demon has slipped up at some point. After all, no one can play their part perfectly. Not even perfect liars. <br /> <br /> Hopefully these questions can encourage paranoid players/characters to become more involved.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also in regard to the ghost part in the adventure. I'm inclined to read that as a mistake or a suggestion that the ghost is somehow, very reasonably, aware of the PC's demonic nature. As there is nothing else in the book to indicate that supernaturals - ghosts or otherwise - can recognize a demon as a demon with very little effort.... Aside from Going Loud and other obvious things like that.<br /> There are also many, many instances in the text which indicate that demons are extremely good at appearing to run-of-the-mill humans or at the very least NOT demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1930-rixx","name":"Rixx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T14:01:25-08:00","id":60113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/57341-spoofing-and-aether?p=59277#post59277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool, hope that works for you. Personally, I'm going to keep the trust issues including the inability to tell each other apart, leave it up to the players to figure out how they know each other and why they'd work together (or at least associate) and tell the players OOC that they're going to have to be extra proactive because there isn't any Prince to appeal to, there isn't a list of rings in the area, and dealing with agencies can be risky. In other words, the players -are- the authority.</div> </div> </div> </div>Without any justification for them to start knowing each other, it's very, very hard to work this out. Look, I can see people becoming allies. I can also see that they will keep their secrets to themselves, as they aren't keen on compromising their covers, potenttially. Either they start asking for any people they imagine could be demons if they are like them, or I cannot conceive how they are going to approach that. <br /> <br /> I am not talking about princes and such, not a society in this sense. Even if there are demons, it's very hard to know their allegiance as such. I am talking about organizations such as agencies, that are on the book, and are very hard to justity, if demons are blind to themselves. Knowing about other demons won't make you trust or like them (if you're smart), but at least, it's a start. Going to Burn Notice, Michael did know at least who some of the players in the city were. It was a start.<br /> <br /> Heck, going to the adventure, they have to contrieve ways to get the characters involved there. It sure needs adjustment. <br /> <br /> There are potential allies out there to trust (or to manipulate), assets to cultivate and information to learn, but it's on the players to find all that. Demon society functionally doesn't really exist in most places, and it certainly doesn't owe you anything by dint of a shared rebellion against the God-Machine.[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> But at least they are players in the spy game that you know you can interact. That's what makes a game. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Demons aren't blind, and they aren't stupid. They can apply their own habits to others and begin looking for incongruities. Demons and Angels can't always perfectly hide-if Demons could, compromise wouldn't be an issue, and if angels could, demons would really be fucked. So a demon is going to see something sooner and later, and they can act on it-follow them, find out information, and set something up. </div> </div> </div>Demons get compromise, amongst other ways, when they go blurting their nature to mortals. They can also get recycled when they blurt their nature to angels, of course. I suppose that demons aren't exactly common, either, that you'd get to be a close acquaintance enough of one to accrue their details enough to guess if they are demon or not. Also, perfect liers, natch. They won't be making involuntary ticks to give themselves up, if they don't want to. <br /> <br /> It's easier to find werewolves and vampires than other demons. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And even if you do sit on your ass, Demonic nature demands inevitable changes in Cover. That might be covered by regular XP, but often times you'll need to make a pact, and that's a blip of standing the hell out, just enough for people to notice. </div> </div> </div>How come pacts are compromising? I suppose you could notice if people are getting rich fast, but... people get lucky all the time, and the contractees sure as hell won't want to divulge the secret of their success. Also, the fae, etc, can make pacts, just as well.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sooner or later, someone is going to see you, and regardless of them being friend or foe, the situation is in their hands. You might as well be proactive, take some chances, and try and make friends at gunpoint. That way, even if you did screw it up, you have more control over the scenario.<br /> <br /> Rebellion is a gamble. Someone who doesn't want to play the game should never have broken the rules in the first place. </div> </div> </div>If you play your cards right, you can be secretive all your life, no big trouble about that. And not demon falls because of a concious choice, of course. Some of them just fail. I can imagine that Demons that want to take than the GMC directly have a bigger chance of going loud, but darwinistic selection would make that most demons would be so deep undercover, they wouldn't get out. Now, if other demons know you are a demon, well, now you a a moving target. Get moving, or get dead.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T15:25:22-08:00","id":60174,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/57341-spoofing-and-aether?p=59932#post59932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Demons aren't blind, and they aren't stupid. They can apply their own habits to others and begin looking for incongruities. Demons and Angels can't always perfectly hide-if Demons could, compromise wouldn't be an issue, and if angels could, demons would really be fucked. So a demon is going to see something sooner and later, and they can act on it-follow them, find out information, and set something up.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/57341-spoofing-and-aether?p=60113#post60113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demons get compromise, amongst other ways, when they go blurting their nature to mortals. They can also get recycled when they blurt their nature to angels, of course. I suppose that demons aren't exactly common, either, that you'd get to be a close acquaintance enough of one to accrue their details enough to guess if they are demon or not. Also, perfect liers, natch. They won't be making involuntary ticks to give themselves up, if they don't want to.<br /> <br /> It's easier to find werewolves and vampires than other demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>A demon does not have to &quot;blurt their nature to mortals.&quot; - or to anyone for that matter - to produce a compromise.<br /> <br /> On page 114 there is a system in place for investigating a demon. If a mortal investigator uses this system - and they succeed - they will provoke a compromise.<br /> NOTE: A demon can use this system on another demon. While this does not cause a compromise. It allows a demon to come up with enough information to compromise the cover if shared with a human.<br /> <br /> ERGO. If you suspect that someone is a demon, you can attempt to dig up the dirt on them. If you succeed, you can cause compromise or have enough leverage to get them to be honest with you.<br /> <br /> It is also worth it to note that a demon knows when their cover has been compromised. HOWEVER the demon doesn't necessarily know the circumstances around the compromise.<br /> <br /> So if a mortal for whatever reason used this system to come up with enough information to compromise the demon AND the demon fails their compromise roll the demon becomes aware that their cover was compromised and nothing else.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, in regards to perfect liars. A demon can tell any lie and make it sound like the truth and they can control their involuntary tics, yes. This is all true.<br /> But if someone relayed a piece of information to me as the truth that flew in the face of other information which I also believed was true, I would be sceptical at the very least. (i.e. I am standing in my yard with my friend who tells me - with the words ringing of truth - that it was raining outside, in my city at my address. It does not matter how perfectly they delivered the lie.)<br /> <br /> In regards for discovering if someone is a werewolf or a vampire compared to other demons, I feel that this is a moot point since the source material makes it clear that it is Extremely Difficult to discern a person's demonic nature and that point is not really up for debate here.<br /> <br /> EDIT: My apologies. It looks like this has gone a bit off-topic. Attempting to bring it back to topic:<br /> <br /> So there are systems in place to deal with discovering demons without having to resort to a blanket &quot;like-knows-like&quot; rule or ... something about Aetheric resonance. ugh, my bad. Still off topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1930,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1930-rixx","user":"Rixx","date":". 01-28-2014, 06:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1930-rixx","name":"Rixx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T21:47:50-08:00","id":60451,"title":"","content":"I think some people are mistaking compromises for Compromises.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T00:02:08-08:00","id":60530,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">I'm going to keep this constrained to the reply towards me I don't have a lot of time and I'm not feeling well, so I'm going to let you guys know I might come back and address the general points already raised.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">(Also, you can stop citing the adventure to me, because I haven't read it and don't plan to. I'm sure it's fine - although if ghosts somehow know demons are demons, then it's already treading down paths I don't particularly want to go - but I've always found that WW adventures are iffy on presenting the game they've written even in the best cases. Not saying you're wrong for citing it, I'm just letting you know that it's falling on deaf ears in my case so you can save yourself some effort.)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/57341-spoofing-and-aether?p=60113#post60113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Without any justification for them to start knowing each other, it's very, very hard to work this out. Look, I can see people becoming allies. I can also see that they will keep their secrets to themselves, as they aren't keen on compromising their covers, potentially. Either they start asking for any people they imagine could be demons if they are like them, or I cannot conceive how they are going to approach that.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">It\u2019s not easy, but I\u2019d like you to consider a few things:</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">1) The common thing that all demons have in common interest-wise is that they all are keeping their eyes open and their ears on the movements of the God-Machine. It\u2019s a lot easier to notice a pattern and to pick out possible candidates when you have a good idea of what drives the pattern. If regular people can track people down through that - and as Rixx mentioned, they can - other Unchained are going to have an easier time, seeing as they a)have better context for what they\u2019re chasing, b)they\u2019re more resistant to the tools demons have to throw them off the trail and c)have plenty of tools of their own to help out. Quick example: pretty easy to remember that you\u2019ve seen a person around two different instances of Infrastructure when you have a perfect memory. A demon who uses Aetheric Resonance can pick out any demon or angel who spends Essence or Aether, uses a demonic form in whole or in part, etc. Two or more demons each using Aetheric Resonance will make each other as Unchained quite handily.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">2) The younger a demon is, the harder it has to work to keep it\u2019s head down because most don\u2019t have the skills or the tools to blend in incredibly. I figure most introductions into demon \u201csociety\u201d start early on, simply because they get picked out of the crowd, taught the ropes, invited into/shuffled off into a ring if they want and then left alone to their own devices. I\u2019d imagine this is especially common when an angel\u2019s fall is dramatic and both loyalists and Unchained race to find the newly Fallen.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Even considering those two points though, you\u2019re correct in that it\u2019s still far from easy. In fact, if a demon is going out of it\u2019s way to make sure it\u2019s not going to be found out, I\u2019m willing to say that in most cases it\u2019s not going to <i>be</i> found out without an <i>enormous</i> amount of effort, patience, and luck. That\u2019s why I believe that...</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">3) Most connection and participation in Unchained \u201csociety\u201d is voluntary. Whether it\u2019s because they want companionship with those who understand what they\u2019re going through, they think that the best way to their goals is with more boots on the ground, or that it\u2019s going to be easier to avoid the God-Machine with multiple people watching out and pooling resources, there are plenty of reasons for a demon to take risks (great and small) to initiate contact, even if it\u2019s to arrange a dead drop or to write a time, a phone number and a name to accept a call with in Arabic on a hotel business card. If all a demon need to stake out a neighborhood or a business as under their protection is a name like Mr. Silver and a phone number, well, a small risk to establish some amount of presence could be just what they need. Which leads straight into...</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I am not talking about princes and such, not a society in this sense. Even if there are demons, it's very hard to know their allegiance as such. I am talking about organizations such as agencies, that are on the book, and are very hard to justity, if demons are blind to themselves. Knowing about other demons won't make you trust or like them (if you're smart), but at least, it's a start. Going to Burn Notice, Michael did know at least who some of the players in the city were. It was a start. </div> </div> </div>In my opinion a lot of reason agencies are both easily available to demons and that they\u2019re treated as a constant security risk is because they\u2019ve taken steps to be easy to found by interested parties. They want members and customers, so while it\u2019s not like you can find them in the yellow pages, by and large you can find a phone number and a <i>nom de enfer</i> for an agency contact with little trouble.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But at least they are players in the spy game that you know you can interact. That's what makes a game. </div> </div> </div>Putting all my cards on the table: I already said that I totally understand why you\u2019d make the change, and I\u2019m cool with it. The main reason why I want to keep it is as secret as it is because I believe that a society of demons that can identify each other on sight is going to be the same, in broad strokes, as Changeling (well, if Changeling\u2019s society was more based on deailng with threats right outside as opposed to in Arcadia, and if there weren\u2019t magic promises to fall back on - look, I said broad strokes, okay). And while Lost\u2019s society is cool, I don\u2019t particularly want to repeat it either.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Besides, I think you\u2019re underestimating just how gameable the setup really is, especially if you start up the game with the ring knowing each other (and figuring out how) and each member knowing at least the name and phone number of another Unchained in town, as well as some basic information on an agency if you want.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T10:04:25-08:00","id":60873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/57341-spoofing-and-aether?p=60530#post60530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Also, you can stop citing the adventure to me, because I haven't read it and don't plan to. I'm sure it's fine - although if ghosts somehow know demons are demons, then it's already treading down paths I don't particularly want to go - but I've always found that WW adventures are iffy on presenting the game they've written even in the best cases. Not saying you're wrong for citing it, I'm just letting you know that it's falling on deaf ears in my case so you can save yourself some effort.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Isaac can\u2019t tell the characters much about Simon, other than what he\u2019s observed about his behavior and that he is a demon (Isaac doesn\u2019t use the word, but he recognizes through aura and mannerisms that the characters and Simon are of a kind).&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T10:25:56-08:00","id":60894,"title":"","content":"First off, Rixx, I wasn't talking to you about the compromises, I was talking to Pcon.<br /> <br /> With that out of the way...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/57341-spoofing-and-aether?p=60113#post60113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demons get compromise, amongst other ways, when they go blurting their nature to mortals. They can also get recycled when they blurt their nature to angels, of course. I suppose that demons aren't exactly common, either, that you'd get to be a close acquaintance enough of one to accrue their details enough to guess if they are demon or not. Also, perfect liers, natch. They won't be making involuntary ticks to give themselves up, if they don't want to.<br /> <br /> It's easier to find werewolves and vampires than other demons.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> How come pacts are compromising? I suppose you could notice if people are getting rich fast, but... people get lucky all the time, and the contractees sure as hell won't want to divulge the secret of their success. Also, the fae, etc, can make pacts, just as well.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If you play your cards right, you can be secretive all your life, no big trouble about that. And not demon falls because of a concious choice, of course. Some of them just fail. I can imagine that Demons that want to take than the GMC directly have a bigger chance of going loud, but darwinistic selection would make that most demons would be so deep undercover, they wouldn't get out. Now, if other demons know you are a demon, well, now you a a moving target. Get moving, or get dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>1)Not all compromises are Compromises. They don't trigger the subroutines that are looking for you or even necessarily have anything to do with your cover. It's just-bam, you're out there to the people who are looking. In the short fiction at the beginning of the section &quot;What Do Demons Do All Day&quot;, a demon checks a safebox. THat's not a Compromise, but for those who know what to look for who have a willingness to investigate everything, it's a compromise.<br /> <br /> Kirby already said it magnificently, so I'll just state-if you want to actually live as a demon, you're going to do things that stand out. That grounds to begin setting up controleld situations to find out more.<br /> <br /> 2)THe Fae can make contracts with the spoken word, with promises and tongue-twisting. Demons need to write that shit out.<br /> <br /> When was the last time you made a deal with someone outside of a business transaction where they wanted you to sign a paper on it? Most people don't go around doing that, and it doesn't help that a written contract brings greater weight to it's reality than something spoken.<br /> <br /> Pacts may not ping supernatural senses, but because of the lengths you'd have to go to make that actually happen, people who are looking will see it happening.<br /> <br /> 3)In other words, you want a demon who does nothing?<br /> <br /> Here's the thing:<br /> <br /> You just want to settle down, live a normal life, raise a family. But you know the God Machine has uses for kids, and your daughter has two colored eyes, making her doubly useful. You don't want her to fall into the God Machine's plans. So, you need to know where it is, so you can tell your children to never go there. Finding out where those places are? To anyone watching, you'll trip some alarms.<br /> <br /> You live by yourself. Fuck most anything, you're just gonna turtle up, nicely disappear. But you ain't gonna traipse through God's territory-however good you may be, there's always the risk you'll show something off. So you go out of your way to avoid the territory. To anyone watching, that will stand out.<br /> <br /> The God Machine is fucking doing something. You can see the infrastructure expanding, the angels moving. You move through them, you're damn good, but that doesn't stop the sense of unease. People are disappearing. Things are getting bad. You could skip town, let it all go to shit here. You could sit here and hope it's not that bad, even though it clearly is. Or you can do something about it. Doing the first or the third will, to anyone watching, trip some alarms. Doing the second one? Well, let's hope your lie holds.<br /> <br /> It's small things, things most of us wouldn't even think about. That's how it was in the Cold War, small things most of us wouldn't even consider. To those watching, demons and angels alike, it is a trigger worth checking on and following, possibly forever. It is worth manipulating and building on.<br /> <br /> Here's the truth about the World of Darkness, the one we don't talk about-nothing can really hide. By sheer dint of awareness, nevermind being different in any other way, you will always do something that sets you apart. For most people, it will never be enough to check, but to those who are watching, it might be.<br /> <br /> Plus, I think you're forgetting that demons fall for personal reasons. Yeah sometimes they fail, but they respond to that in some way, be it &quot;Oh God, take me back&quot; or &quot;&quot;Oh shit, gotta hide from Daddy&quot;, but you respond to your fall, and it often otivates you to act in some way to the God Machine, nevermind the people around you. If you act in regards to something, even if it's hiding from someone, you create an environment that revolves around the thing you're reacting to, and that is something that can be followed. THe best people at hide and seek are not the people who hide from the seeker, but just go off and read a book.<br /> <br /> Point is, even if it's not a Compromise, Demons compromise themselves in a lot of ways, and set themselves up to be acted upon one way or another. Unless you act back, nine times out of ten you're screwed.<br /> <br /> Rebellion is a gamble, even unintentional rebellion. It's better to make friends at gun point than to sit all by yourself. And above all else,<br /> <br /> <i>You can never really hide</i>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T10:34:19-08:00","id":60897,"title":"","content":"Actually, simple version: Did you even really read the Moscow Rules and consider what that all truly implies?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T17:10:53-08:00","id":61173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/57341-spoofing-and-aether?p=60897#post60897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, simple version: Did you even really read the Moscow Rules and consider what that all truly implies?</div> </div> </div> </div>Short version: yes. The way I read it, it implies that you should trust no one, as you are in hostile territory. Go, do your mission, don't ever let your true nature be known, or you will be taken down. That, of couse, can be a problem. <br /> <br /> Not trying to fight the forum system to attempt multi-quoting again, but you asked me if I wanted a demon that doesn't do anything. That exactly what I don't want! I know that some players tendo to be paranoid, very much so. I wouldn't want to have characters that would interact with nobody, and the way I see, it's a very distinct possibility. Even if the players know their own nature, they could live as an island. I don't think that's desirable, IMO. <br /> <br /> About this making a bland society, I'm not so sure. First of all, there are plenty of loyalists, so people wouldn't want to live in a court, or something that would make them such an easy target. But, they would like to check themselves up, and a pipeline for information and reputation would work. You know, much like an intelligence community work in the spy stories. One demon gets caught, and after awhile, everybody knows that an angel is around. Things like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T17:22:27-08:00","id":61183,"title":"","content":"Oh, and about investigating potential demons. It takes time, and you have to have something to start. You won't go much far checking people randomly, so where would you begin? Even young demons can go silent pretty easily. <br /> <br /> \u200bDemons that Go Loud can get a lot of attention, of course. But they don't tend to last, if that's the way they go. And even going loud won't make such a perturbation on a medium size town. You're still not likely to notice. And if youi did, would you want to associate yourself with someone like that? If you're gung ho yourself, perhaps, othwerwise, I'm not so sure. But then, making other demons know themselves when them meet is still preferable to having to wait someone go destroy a cover, IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T12:32:57-08:00","id":61669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/57341-spoofing-and-aether?p=61183#post61183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then, making other demons know themselves when them meet is still preferable to having to wait someone go destroy a cover, IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would destroy a lot of the paranoia, though. How can you be sure that your Cover's girlfriend is <i>really</i> your Cover's girlfriend and not some demon who patched that relationship into his <i>own</i> Cover to keep tabs on you? Well, if you can recognize a fellow demon on sight, that's pretty trivial, isn't it?<br /> <br /> And demons hardly need to Go Loud to be noticed. There are all sorts of things a demon cares about that an average human wouldn't, the God-Machine being the most obvious. Maybe you meet up while sabotaging the same bit of Infrastructure, get forced to team up to fight off the defense systems, and end up with a wary sort of alliance of convenience. Maybe some Stigmatic prophet hooks you up. The point is, demons will have certain interests in common, and they can use those interests to pick each other out from the crowd.<br /> <br /> Now, I suppose you <i>could</i> posit a demon who <i>doesn't</i> have any interests beyond hiding from the God-Machine, who spends every moment ready to drop everything at the slightest hint of compromise, and who never, ever, ever does anything to draw attention to himself. I can't imagine any ST actually letting you <i>play</i> such an abomination, though: We're talking about a group activity here. Who knows? Maybe the world <i>is</i> full of ultra-cautious demons who perfectly slip into their covers, living mortal lives and dying mortal deaths, never giving a hint as to their true natures... but if so, the game isn't about them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1369-mewtarthio","name":"Mewtarthio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T15:03:29-08:00","id":61762,"title":"","content":"But the real paranoia is not about the other demons. It's the angels, it's the GM. So, your girlfriend could be a demon. That's one hell of an effort, when they could just, you know, denouce you to a GMC headquarter. Or, you know, turning your girlfirend in a double agent, which has all the benefits of becoming your girlfirend, without having to spend all the time doing that. Oh, and if you meet a demon on the street, what do you do? He might be a turncoat. Will he sell your hide to save his? Will he blackmail you into joining his agency, or taking a hit at an angel that's getting too close? Will both of you start investigating each other at a distance, so you know if you are trustworthy? It just opens a lot of possibilities! <br /> <br /> Not all demons go to take down infrastructure. And if they do, they will tend to take care of not being noticed, by GM and his angels, and therefore also by you. Either way, you will have to be investigating the infrastructure when the other demon acts, and not be noticed yourself. In other words, if you noticed the demon, GM also has, probably. Want to join the club? And that's IF you are one of the inclination, and that's about 2/5 of angels, give or take. <br /> <br /> Demons have many interests besides attacking the GM, and they are as diverse as demons are. Protecting someone, learning about the world, the occult, having fun, taking down the chinese mafia. You name it. They are not a GM monomaniacal block. It's just too chancy to have demons that will have common interests and slip up enough for each to consider the other is a demon (instead of just a weird guy). Let's say they are pretty common, as far as supernatural being go, and are 1 in 10,000. How likely that consumate liars that want to take care of their cover first of all will notice each other?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T15:24:46-08:00","id":61774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/57341-spoofing-and-aether?p=61762#post61762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demons have many interests besides attacking the GM</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're not watching the thing that wants to cannibalize you for spare parts like the malfunctioning unit you are, you are not long for the Descent. It's like living in front of a busy interstate and refusing to look both ways, and also the interstate is some significant percentage used by gangsters fully prepared to pull a drive-by if they think you're around. You'd have to be a pretty colossal idiot not to at least keep an eye open.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How likely that consumate liars that want to take care of their cover first of all will notice each other? </div> </div> </div>Assuming they're still using Embeds and Exploits and making pacts? Pretty likely in the long run, even without the option of investigating them to see if it pings their Cover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T22:57:11-08:00","id":62008,"title":"","content":"APOLOGIES FOR THE WALL OF TEXT<br /> <br /> TL<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />R version<br /> <br /> Infrastructure security varies<br /> Infrastructure should interest all demons in some capacity not just 2/5<br /> &quot;Demons have many interests IN ADDITION to the God Machine&quot;<br /> Demons should always consider the god machine<br /> Example of two demons interacting in an area of similar interest<br /> Mr. Bee comes away from the exchanges with an idea that Ms. Aigh is a demon<br /> Both acted completely in-character (or rather both acted in cover)<br /> Perfect lying may have occurred from Ms. Aigh to Mr. Bee.<br /> Ms. Aigh's perfect lie does not supersede Mr. Bee's critical thinking.<br /> Cheers!<br /> Rixx<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/57341-spoofing-and-aether?p=61762#post61762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not all demons go to take down infrastructure. And if they do, they will tend to take care of not being noticed, by GM and his angels, and therefore also by you. Either way, you will have to be investigating the infrastructure when the other demon acts, and not be noticed yourself. In other words, if you noticed the demon, GM also has, probably. Want to join the club? And that's IF you are one of the inclination, and that's about 2/5 of angels, give or take.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree with the parallel you've drawn regarding demon discovery at infrastructure and God-Machine discovery.at infrastructure.<br /> As I understand your point, it appears that If X knows this then Y knows this (probably).<br /> I am not sure how you're arriving at this as the security in place at infrastructure varies.based on a variety of factors (i.e. size, purpose, location, importance, etc., of the infrastructure).<br /> It is my understanding that not every piece of infrastructure need be some kind of Mission Impossible complex and that some places are, perhaps, more akin to a guard post with a guard whose attention wanders.<br /> <br /> this &quot;2/5 of angels&quot; number is also somewhat confusing, I'm not sure to what 'inclination' you're speaking of. What angels, exacly, are you referring to? If perhaps you meant, demons, then what demons are you referring to? Saboteurs and Integrators???<br /> <br /> My reading of it is 2/5's of demons are inclined to investigate infrastructure. Based upon that reading I'd have to disagree (Also, my apologies if I've mis-read your intent but 2/5 seems to two agencies out of five possible agency choices (inquisitors, tempters, saboteurs, integrators, undeclared... or whatever it is they're called). I'll get to it in a second.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/57341-spoofing-and-aether?p=61762#post61762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demons have many interests besides attacking the GM,</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm also inclined to disagree with this statement as well. Perhaps this is quibbling but maybe it's a better characterization to say that demons have many interests IN ADDITION to the God-Machine.<br /> <br /> The G-M and whether or not a demon violently responds to actions taken by the G-M is something every demon should be considering. How often, how long and how deeply each demon considers their conflict with the G-M varies with each demon but it is my belief that this conflict should not be far from a demon's mind EVEN WHEN they are pursuing interests that may not relate to the G-M at first glance because [paranoia] the G-M or its agents can be anyone or anything anywhere at any given time. [/paranoia]<br /> <br /> Apologies for the scare-mongering. If the G-M can be potentially anyone or potentially anything if one isn't devoting a good portion of their attention to the G-M and countermeasures to take if the person or thing they are dealing with is an agent of the G-M. then perhaps their rebellion is short-lived.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/57341-spoofing-and-aether?p=61762#post61762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>How likely that consumate liars that want to take care of their cover first of all will notice each other?</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I mentioned perfect liars earlier. Perhaps I'll take an opportunity to clarify but first I want to make this point.<br /> <br /> I think that many people have already stated this in varying ways but I suppose I'll state it again: <b><i>YOU CAN BE DISCOVERED AS A DEMON EVEN IF YOU ARE ACTING COMPLETELY WITHIN YOUR COVER IF SOMEONE, LIKE ANOTHER FELLOW DEMON, KNOWS WHAT TO LOOK FOR.</i></b><br /> <br /> -----Example time:I am role-playing a life coach (Ms. Aigh) who deals with people who desperately want to change something about themselves. They want to become more successful, lose weight, get the (gender of their choice), and so on.<br /> <br /> Ms. Aigh also gets her clients to sign an agreement that, among other things, gets the clients to commit 100% of their being to achieving their goals. MIND, BODY AND SOUL. They must give me their all when I help them pursue theses goals.Absolutely everything. No reservations, no hesitation.<br /> <br /> Right there, Ms. Aigh has got a number of poor unfortunate souls (IN PAIN! IN NEED!) to soul pact with her. And so far nothing really sticks out.<br /> <br /> Ms. Aigh still helps the people who don't sign (or maybe she doesn't, but let's say she does) and perhaps they succeed or not. And perhaps Ms. Aigh doesn't soul pact everyone by changing the words very slightly and reserving the soul pacts for covers she is really interested in.<br /> At the very worst, Ms. Aigh is perhaps considered slightly melodramatic, maybe a bit dire as a life coach, -shrug- nothing that raises much attention.<br /> <br /> However, to another demon (Mr. Bee) who is interested in a set-up like Ms. Aigh's (even though at this point in the example they consider her a human.) comes through her door in one of his covers to investigate Ms. Aigh and her business.<br /> <br /> Mr. Bee manages to meet with Ms Aigh (he still think she's human) and they have some interactions where they discuss Mr. Bee's situation (again, neither of know that the other is a demon at this point).<br /> <br /> Then it comes time for Mr. Bee to make the commitment, Ms. Aigh gets out the contract, (As a demon, Mr. Bee is always interested in contracts so this raises a flag and he pays close attention) and they go over terms. Mr. Bee makes excuses (perfectly executed lies) and refuses to sign the contract at that moment. Perhaps Mr. Bee questions Ms. Aigh on the contract and Ms. Aigh creates a perfectly believable explanation (which is a perfectly executed lie). Perhaps Mr. Bee makes another appointment to return, maybe he doesn't but <u><b>he's met Ms. Aigh, seen what she does and seen one of her contracts</b></u>.<br /> <br /> Mr. Bee returns to his lair/safe place/cover's house/whatever and reviews Ms. Aigh's contract thanks to his Eidetic Memory. Mr. Bee discovers that the contract contains provisions which would essentially make a human promise their soul to Ms. Aigh in exchange for her assistance to help the mortal achieve their goals.<br /> <br /> Mr. Bee quickly gains the strong suspicion that Ms. Aigh is a demon as well. It makes sense, <u><b>He was contemplating a similar set-up</b></u>.<br /> <br /> -----END EXAMPLE-----<br /> <br /> So, we have two perfect liars who have just interacted with each other and without acting out of character at all and taking reasonable steps to maintain their cover Ms. Aigh might have been discovered as a demon.<br /> <br /> <br /> So what does this mean?<br /> You are always susceptible to discovery. Especially by others who are aware of the habits of your kind (I'M SURE this point has been made before).<br /> <br /> In this way we also see that the ability to lie perfectly has not prevented another person from strongly suspecting the other's demonic identity.<br /> <br /> Yes demons are perfect liars. No argument, RAW, source material supported, etc.,.<br /> <u><b>Your lie may still be questioned even if it appears to be the truth.</b></u><br /> <br /> <u><i><b>A perfect ability to lie does not supersede, override or otherwise impair another person's ability to critically think, question or just be stubborn.</b></i></u><br /> <br /> If Ms. Aigh had perfectly explained away the process it doesn't change Mr. Bee's ability to read the contract, think on the terms and (hopefully if he's any good) recognize the terms for what they were.<br /> <br /> Now this example isn't perfect. Perhaps you disagree with my very rough approximation of a soul pact, I'm not trying to sell you on on the validity of my terms of the soul pact, just the idea that Ms. Aigh can use this position to get soul pacts from many people.<br /> <br /> Perhaps Ms. Aigh did not give Mr. Bee a contract with soul pact terms. It is still likely that Mr. Bee considers the possibility that Ms. Aigh is a demon <b>because he, a reasonable demon, has considered a similar operation</b>. Mr. Bee, in this instance has less to go on but decides to do more research to get more information on another demon who may be a potential rival or ally. <br /> <br /> Perhaps you disagree with another point and that's fair too.<br /> <br /> HOWEVERI do hope this adequately addresses the concerns about perfect lying and detection by another while maintaining a cover.<br /> <br /> If you've made it to the end, THANK YOU! apologies for the text wall and Cheers!<br /> Rixx","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1930,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1930-rixx","user":"Rixx","date":". 01-31-2014, 02:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1930-rixx","name":"Rixx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T13:47:50-08:00","id":62442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/57341-spoofing-and-aether?p=61762#post61762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the real paranoia is not about the other demons. It's the angels, it's the GM. So, your girlfriend could be a demon. That's one hell of an effort, when they could just, you know, denouce you to a GMC headquarter. Or, you know, turning your girlfirend in a double agent, which has all the benefits of becoming your girlfirend, without having to spend all the time doing that.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are plenty of reasons a demon might want to infiltrate the life of another demon. Maybe he wants to manipulate the sap into testing out some Infrastructure's defenses. Maybe the two have competing agendas. Regardless, there <i>are</i> reasons it would happen. And going to the God-Machine is a very bad idea for most demons, while human double agents are nowhere near as good at it as demons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh, and if you meet a demon on the street, what do you do? He might be a turncoat. Will he sell your hide to save his? Will he blackmail you into joining his agency, or taking a hit at an angel that's getting too close? Will both of you start investigating each other at a distance, so you know if you are trustworthy? It just opens a lot of possibilities! </div> </div> </div>None of those possibilities go away if demon's <i>don't</i> recognize each other on sight. Just replace &quot;you meet a demon on the street&quot; with &quot;you discover that someone else is really a demon.&quot; Adding an automatic Detect Demon ability cuts out more story possibilities than it adds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1369-mewtarthio","name":"Mewtarthio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-08T02:59:06-08:00","id":67812,"title":"","content":"As a deviation from the most recent discussion but still on the topic of covers, does investigating a cover work if the cover is not currently in use? If so, does it still cause a compromise? And if it does do the conditions attach to the cover the demon is currently wearing or only when the demon switches back to the cover that was investigated?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2108-genesis","name":"genesis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T05:41:22-08:00","id":68992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>genesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/57341-spoofing-and-aether?p=67812#post67812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a deviation from the most recent discussion but still on the topic of covers, does investigating a cover work if the cover is not currently in use? If so, does it still cause a compromise? And if it does do the conditions attach to the cover the demon is currently wearing or only when the demon switches back to the cover that was investigated?</div> </div> </div> </div>The system set out on page 114 doesn't differentiate between active and inactive covers. It seems to me that the investigation would revolve around a specific cover. <br /> If a human succeeds in their investigation then the demon must check for cover as if they &quot;revealed a key fact about themselves&quot; to the human.<br /> Since the human is investigating a specific cover, the demon should roll that specific cover's dice on the compromise roll. <br /> The conditions listed on page 118 attach to a specific cover so they should attach to the cover that was under investigation. However, some of those conditions can interfere with your demon regardless of whatever covers they're wearing; like the Hunted condition.<br /> <br /> So example time, ------<br /> One of your covers, Ms. Bitters, somehow draws the attention of a crazy conspiracy theorist. The conspiracy nut thinks that something is off about Ms. Bitters and starts turning his investigations toward the weird. The conspiracy nut may have already done some normal investigation but your cover stood up to that. Either way he starts investigating using the rules on page 114 and he succeeds.<br /> <br /> Now, when he succeeds you are currently Mr. Christopher and have not been Ms. Bitters in days. But since the conspiracy nut was investigating Ms. Bitters, you roll Ms. Bitters cover (let's say, 5) against the compromise roll instead of Mr. Christopher's (which is, let's say... 8). <br /> Unfortunately you fail and get to choose between flagged, surveilled and hunted. (or roll for permanent glitch). So let's say you choose Hunted.<br /> <br /> Even though Ms. Bitters has the hunted condition. Angels have been dispatched to look for a demon in the area. Now you (as Mr. Christopher) AND any other demons in the area where you operate are put at risk even though the Ms. Bitters cover is the one that was investigated.<br /> <br /> ----END----<br /> <br /> It is also worth noting that if you choose to roll a glitch that glitches attach to the demon and not the cover so they persist regardless of whatever meatsuit you're wearing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1930-rixx","name":"Rixx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T03:52:53-07:00","id":99907,"title":"","content":"So, does spoofing prompt a Clash of Wiils against the opposing effect, or is it just an absolute 'if I get a single success it doesn't matter how powerful of an effect is trying to detect me it auto fails' sort of thing. I don't think I like the idea of the latter, so I'm hoping I just missed something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T04:50:28-07:00","id":99921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/57341-spoofing-and-aether?p=99907#post99907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, does spoofing prompt a Clash of Wiils against the opposing effect, or is it just an absolute 'if I get a single success it doesn't matter how powerful of an effect is trying to detect me it auto fails' sort of thing. I don't think I like the idea of the latter, so I'm hoping I just missed something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spoofing hides the demon's true nature and allows them to pass as human. So when you say &quot;detect me&quot; I'm reading that as &quot;detect my supernatural nature directly or by implication&quot; or perhaps &quot;detect me as anything other than human&quot;. It does not render a demon undetectable in general.<br /> <br /> My reading of spoofing is that it should not prompt a clash of wills because the power as it is written already contemplates and resolves an issue in which two supernatural powers clash.<br /> specifically 1) I always appear to be human even in the face of supernatural detection methods and 2) I am detecting whether this person is a human or otherwise..<br /> <br /> I submit that this should not prompt a further test wherein the two supernatural powers roll against each other as that is in effect directly undermining the effect of the spoof.<br /> I further submit that the wording of clash of wills contemplates embeds vs disciplines vs arcana and other such ilk. The clash of wills side-bar is placed immediately before embeds also supports this.<br /> The clash of wills section is also silent regarding cover and detection because, in my view, it has already been adequately addressed by spoofing.<br /> <br /> Of course, you or your story-teller may elect to house-rule that but consider the wider implication.<br /> In an espionage game if every neonate vampire or neophyte mage or newbie anything could activate a low level power and tell that a demon was a demon <b>would really throw a wrench in the whole works.</b><br /> In a higher power game there may be more avenues open to determining that this individual is not a human without the need to resort to supernatural detection.<br /> <br /> Also, spoofing is not a guaranteed thing. It has to be rolled and you must gain 1 success. It can fail.<br /> <br /> In my view, further undermining the usefulness of spoofing does not contribute to better game play. That said, I could see an argument for how the weakening of spoofing could raise more tension for some especially intense espionage narratives but that's only one specific example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1930,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1930-rixx","user":"Rixx","date":".  note to self: don't post before first pot of coffee in the morning. 03-27-2014, 07:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1930-rixx","name":"Rixx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T05:51:09-07:00","id":99945,"title":"","content":"Simply put, I don't like how absolute spoofing is. Sure, I wouldn't mind just making it really hard to do by penalizing rolls and/or out-rolling them as with a Changelings mien, but something as hit or miss as getting just 1 success on a roll that you will usually have quite a few dice in isn't something I care for in my games. This would be like having mind mages only being required to roll a single success on a Wisdom roll to perfectly counter any attempt to read or look into their mind/thoughts, regardless of who or what was attempting to do it or how much power/effort to offending party was putting into it. Simply put, I feel that no limit abilities such as these should remain little more than plot devices.<br /> <br /> I'll probably end up houseruling it to work much more like Changeling, where while really hard to do, can still be done given sufficient skill/effort on the part of whoever's attempting to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T10:57:13-07:00","id":100171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/57341-spoofing-and-aether?p=99945#post99945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simply put, I don't like how absolute spoofing is.</div> </div> </div> </div>The exact same splat we're talking about can lie so perfectly that even abilities that don't check a statement against &quot;is this person lying?&quot; but rather &quot;does this statement describe the truth?&quot; are fooled.<br /> <br /> This aspect is unrolled.<br /> <br /> The beings these supernatural beings come from, meanwhile, have an absolute lockout of any mind control that would cause them to forgo their missions.<br /> <br /> This aspect is also unrolled.<br /> <br /> By comparison, it's relatively easy to fray Cover, and spoofing only extends its scene-long camouflage against individual effects per roll. Put a Cover 7 demon in a room full of other supernaturals with supernatural-detecting abilities (say, a high-Clarity changeling, a vampire with a few dots of Auspex, and a mage with an aura-reading rote, among others) and they'll fail the battery of tests eventually, particularly when some Covers can be frayed just by keeping the demon from his appointments.<br /> <br /> It's a protection against incidental fuckups that incentivizes raising your Cover. It is not a &quot;no limit ability.&quot; Cover as a dicepool is limited to ten dice at most and it's much easier to lower it than to raise it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T15:59:49-07:00","id":100429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/57341-spoofing-and-aether?p=100171#post100171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The exact same splat we're talking about can lie so perfectly that even abilities that don't check a statement against &quot;is this person lying?&quot; but rather &quot;does this statement describe the truth?&quot; are fooled.<br /> <br /> This aspect is unrolled.<br /> <br /> The beings these supernatural beings come from, meanwhile, have an absolute lockout of any mind control that would cause them to forgo their missions.<br /> <br /> This aspect is also unrolled.<br /> <br /> By comparison, it's relatively easy to fray Cover, and spoofing only extends its scene-long camouflage against individual effects per roll. Put a Cover 7 demon in a room full of other supernaturals with supernatural-detecting abilities (say, a high-Clarity changeling, a vampire with a few dots of Auspex, and a mage with an aura-reading rote, among others) and they'll fail the battery of tests eventually, particularly when some Covers can be frayed just by keeping the demon from his appointments.<br /> <br /> It's a protection against incidental fuckups that incentivizes raising your Cover. It is not a &quot;no limit ability.&quot; Cover as a dicepool is limited to ten dice at most and it's much easier to lower it than to raise it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll be honest, I don't really care much for the can't be caught lying aspect either tbqh, and may or may not (leaning towards not actually) change that. As for angels and mind control, that is perfectly fine, because as it was described somewhere (can't remember if it was in the book or on the forums), but since they're connected to the God-Machine, for all intents and purposes you are rolling against it and it is assumed that it out-rolls you. And that's fine, the God-Machine is a being powerful enough to be little more than a plot device so I'm fine with that. That said, I'd probably even throw the absolute nature of that out the window against other sufficiently powerful beings such as the Principle, the Gentry when in Arcadia, Gaea, or the Exarchs.<br /> <br /> As for the ol' 'lets see if you can survive the gauntlet or dice' scenario, I don't think I know any ST who would want to bog the game down long enough to make 20 rolls all checking to see the same thing when it comes to something like this. This is what group rolls are for.<br /> <br /> In the end, the problem isn't even how many or how few dice you get, it's that the ability has no interactions. It doesn't matter who/what/how power/how skilled/or how much time and effort is going into the other side of things, if you roll a single success, you trump the effect. And things like that simply aren't that interesting from a story or mechanical perspective imo.<br /> <br /> Edit: After thinking more about the first part, I'm somewhat ok with the lying thing in that they can decide whether or not what they say rings true or not, but I'll probably change it so that abilities that tell whether something is 'true' or not, not whether they're lying, but if something is 'true', will still work. The effect is rare enough to not be something that comes up a lot, and to be quite honest, Liar's Tongue even affecting that to begin with doesn't make any sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 03-27-2014, 07:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T16:29:18-07:00","id":100456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/57341-spoofing-and-aether?p=99945#post99945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simply put, I don't like how absolute spoofing is. Sure, I wouldn't mind just making it really hard to do by penalizing rolls and/or out-rolling them as with a Changelings mien, but something as hit or miss as getting just 1 success on a roll that you will usually have quite a few dice in isn't something I care for in my games. This would be like having mind mages only being required to roll a single success on a Wisdom roll to perfectly counter any attempt to read or look into their mind/thoughts, regardless of who or what was attempting to do it or how much power/effort to offending party was putting into it. Simply put, I feel that no limit abilities such as these should remain little more than plot devices.</div> </div> </div> </div> Changeling mein breaking rules were so lopsided and ill designed. If you have to do a different roll, why not just use Clash of Will? This is exactly the kind of situation its meant to cover, I think.<br /> <br /> I think, on the other hand, that a better Mage comparison is their Unseen Senses, which is a bit nasty in that its automatically successful at detecting magical people and powers. Its an equivalent, and diametrically opposed, ability. One detection, one hiding.<br /> <br /> And it probably is a plot device, as the vast majority of demon abilities/powers weren't designed with balance against other supernatural beings in mind. Demons need to be able to hide from the God Machine, who will roll more successes than a lone demon ever could. Angels would be able to detect them without it - Rank 5 hunter angels have insane dice pools.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-27-2014, 07:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T16:51:48-07:00","id":100464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/57341-spoofing-and-aether?p=100456#post100456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Changeling mein breaking rules were so lopsided and ill designed. If you have to do a different roll, why not just use Clash of Will? This is exactly the kind of situation its meant to cover, I think.<br /> <br /> I think, on the other hand, that a better Mage comparison is their Unseen Senses, which is a bit nasty in that its automatically successful at detecting magical people and powers. Its an equivalent, and diametrically opposed, ability. One detection, one hiding.<br /> <br /> And it probably is a plot device, as the vast majority of demon abilities/powers weren't designed with balance against other supernatural beings in mind. Demons need to be able to hide from the God Machine, who will roll more successes than a lone demon ever could. Angels would be able to detect them without it - Rank 5 hunter angels have insane dice pools.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since it's been a while since I've looked through/played changeling take note that I may have meant Mask instead if Mien.<br /> <br /> Anyways, here's the thing, I get that they want to make it really hard to see through, and I'm perfectly fine with that. That said, just a Clash of Wills might make that a little too easy. So I'd be fine with a two-fold defense like in Changeling, where not only do you get to roll off against them, but they're also at a -3 to see you for what you really are. And I'm fine with something like this. Given enough skill from the opposing force when compared to the demon in question the spoof can be overcome.<br /> <br /> Also, needing to hide from the God-Machine isn't much of an excuse tbh. Mages need to hide from the Exarchs, and Changelings need to hide from the Gentry, but they don't get abilities that say if I always roll at least 1 success you can never tell what I am. And before you say it, I already know that their situations aren't exactly the same. The Exarchs and Gentry aren't hunting their splat as doggedly (at least not always) as the angels of the God-Machine, but the point stands, demons aren't the only ones hiding from forces they couldn't possibly stand up to in an all out confrontation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 03-27-2014, 08:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T17:04:28-07:00","id":100470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/57341-spoofing-and-aether?p=100464#post100464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since it's been a while since I've looked through/played changeling take note that I may have meant Mask instead if Mien.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, typo.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyways, here's the thing, I get that they want to make it really hard to see through, and I'm perfectly fine with that. That said, just a Clash of Wills might make that a little too easy. So I'd be fine with a two-fold defense like in Changeling, where not only do you get to roll off against them, but they're also at a -3 to see you for what you really are. And I'm fine with something like this. Given enough skill from the opposing force when compared to the demon in question the spoof can be overcome. </div> </div> </div> Rolling your entire Cover + Power attribute isn't already lopsided enough? Either way, the issue I had with changeling was how the perception rolls from each supernatural were badly picked. Mages with ritual cast mage sight before hand? Werewolves with form perception bonuses? Vampires who had to have a specific discipline active, had a very odd roll picked, and refused to account for any other potential power?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, needing to hide from the God-Machine isn't much of an excuse tbh. Mages need to hide from the Exarchs, and Changelings need to hide from the Gentry, but they don't get abilities that say if I always roll at least 1 success you can never tell what I am. And I hope that remains true in the coming FWC. I love mage to death but I don't want them to have abilities of this nature. That said, if this is really going to become the new standard, I shutter to think what werewolves and especially mages are going going to be capable of come their updates. </div> </div> </div> Mages don't hide from the Exarchs; no proof the Exarchs even truly exist! They hide from the Seers, and they can cloak their spells so it doesn't ping anyone's senses. Changelings have options to strengthen the Mask so that you cannot see through it, no roll from any fae allowed to break it.<br /> <br /> So, if anything, the Demons are the ones who are lopsided, as they need to require a roll. And hiding is the Unchained's forte. Its their specialty, just as magical investigation is Mage's, and hunting is Werewolf's, and mind control is Vampire's.<br /> <br /> As well, mages DO have a &quot;one success that you cannot contest&quot; power. Scrutinizing resonance to read nature, your power, etc. Should we have contested rolls for all Unseen Senses and mage sight scrutiny? Because that's a similiar issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-27-2014, 08:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T17:15:23-07:00","id":100475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/57341-spoofing-and-aether?p=100464#post100464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Mages need to hide from the Exarchs, and Changelings need to hide from the Gentry, but they don't get abilities that say if I always roll at least 1 success you can never tell what I am. And before you say it, I already know that their situations aren't exactly the same. The Exarchs and Gentry aren't hunting their splat as doggedly (at least not always) as the angels of the God-Machine, but the point stands, demons aren't the only ones hiding from forces they couldn't possibly stand up to in an all out confrontation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Simply put, the themes at play surrounding Mage and changeling do not have an emphasis on espionage and the threat of discovery. I concede that THEY COULD have an emphasis on espionage and that those narratives could be fun and interesting to explore in those settings. However, in my view, they are &quot;about&quot; different things.<br /> <br /> Spoofing doesn't need to be &quot;excused&quot;. It is a core mechanic that ties in to the core concepts and themes of the system.<br /> <br /> You are always free to rule as you feel you need to. However, I would caution that changing this mechanic may mean Terrible Things for your demon players and the longevity of their Demon characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1930-rixx","name":"Rixx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T17:30:11-07:00","id":100484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/57341-spoofing-and-aether?p=100470#post100470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yes, typo.<br /> <br /> Rolling your entire Cover + Power attribute isn't already lopsided enough? Either way, the issue I had with changeling was how the perception rolls from each supernatural were badly picked. Mages with ritual cast mage sight before hand? Werewolves with form perception bonuses? Vampires who had to have a specific discipline active, had a very odd roll picked, and refused to account for any other potential power?<br /> <br /> Mages don't hide from the Exarchs; no proof the Exarchs even truly exist! They hide from the Seers, and they can cloak their spells so it doesn't ping anyone's senses. Changelings have options to strengthen the Mask so that you cannot see through it, no roll from any fae allowed to break it.<br /> <br /> So, if anything, the Demons are the ones who are lopsided, as they need to require a roll. And hiding is the Unchained's forte. Its their specialty, just as magical investigation is Mage's, and hunting is Werewolf's, and mind control is Vampire's.<br /> <br /> As well, mages DO have a &quot;one success that you cannot contest&quot; power. Scrutinizing resonance to read nature, your power, etc. Should we have contested rolls for all Unseen Senses and mage sight scrutiny? Because that's a similiar issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I'll agree that the specifics for how they did it was odd, I wasn't really talking exact carry over. Of course I'd tailor it to fit a bit better, but I'm just giving an idea of the direction I'd take. I'd probably have the roll be something like Subterfuge/Stealth/Wits + Cover with the opposition taking a -x penalty to see them for what they are. I'd have to play with numbers to get a set value for what I'm going for but it shouldn't be too hard.<br /> <br /> And mages hide from them both. While the Seers are the main task force, the Exarchs themselves do have the option of getting their hands dirty and dealing with things through their own power, though they typically reserve such actions for when it is really necessary. Spell cloaking also takes Prime 2 and 1 mana and can be pierced by sufficiently powerful effects. And while changelings can strengthen the mask so you can't see their true form, aura/nature reading will still tell you that they're a changeling, you just can't see what they really look like.<br /> <br /> And mages do not have a 'one success that you cannot counter power'. Not only does it take time, scrutinizing is also noticeable. It also has to overcome the potency of any concealing effects the target has on them. So while not directly contested, it is easily resisted by those with the ability to do so unless the mage is powerful enough or has spent enough time and effort to pierce the effect. While I don't think this is in the books, any concealing effect automatically trumps Unseen Senses.<br /> <br /> We've also kind've gone a bit off topic, which is why I edited my first post when I realized it would probably lead to this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 03-27-2014, 08:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}